          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em iso-inserter
            is a particular kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
            in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} invertible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            between a pair of parallel 1-morphisms.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g\colon A\rightrightarrows B
            be a pair of parallel 1-morphisms in a 2-category. The
            %strong iso-inserter
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            is a universal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            equipped with a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\colon V\to A
            and an invertible 2-morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi f
                    %mi v
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≅
                    %mi g
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\colon f v \xrightarrow{\cong} g v
          %p
            More precisely, universality means that for any object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi IsoIns
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X,V) \to IsoIns(Hom(X,f),Hom(X,g))
          %p
            is an equivalence, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi IsoIns
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} IsoIns(Hom(X,f),Hom(X,g))
            denotes the category whose objects are pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi u
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (u,\beta)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u\colon X\to A
            is a morphism and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi f
                  %mi u
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≅
                  %mi g
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta\colon f u \xrightarrow{\cong} g u
            is an invertible 2-morphism. If this functor is an
            %em isomorphism
            of categories, then we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi v
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\xrightarrow{v} A
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong strict iso-inserter
          %p
            Iso-inserters and strict iso-inserters can be described as a certain sort of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted
            2-limit, where the diagram shape is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+structure"} walking
            parallel pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P = (\cdot \rightrightarrows\cdot)
            and the weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to Cat
            is the diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Iso
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \;\rightrightarrows\; Iso
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso
            is the walking
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            An iso-inserter in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+2-category"} opposite 2-category
            %strong co-iso-inserter
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any iso-inserter is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+morphism"} faithful morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+morphism"} conservative morphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+morphism"} fully faithful morphism
            %li
              %p Any strict iso-inserter is, in particular, an iso-inserter. (This is not true for all strict 2-limits.)
            %li
              %p
                Since
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Iso
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conical+limit"} conical limit
                of a diagram of shape
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                = succeed "." do
                  %em pseudo-equalizer
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+pseudolimit"} strict pseudolimit
                of a diagram of shape
                = succeed "\u2014is" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iso-comma-objects"} iso-comma-objects
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-pullbacks"} pseudo-pullbacks
            %li
              %p
                Iso-inserters can be constructed as an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inserter"} inserter
                followed by an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverter"} inverter
                (for both the strict and non-strict versions). In particular, it follows that strict iso-inserters are a type of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PIE-limit"} PIE-limit
        .revisedby
